"title": "Prepositions",
"span": "A1–B2",
"blurb": "σε, από, για, με and the other everyday prepositions, all with the accusative; adverbs that combine with σε and από; and the learned prepositions with the genitive (λόγω, μεταξύ, μέσω).",
"intro": [
{
"p": "Good news: almost every everyday Greek preposition takes the **accusative**. The bad news is that the most frequent ones each have several meanings: **σε** is \"to, in, at, on\", **από** is \"from, since, by, than, through\". Learn them in phrases, not as single words."
},
{
"p": "The learned prepositions of formal Greek (**λόγω, μεταξύ, μέσω, εναντίον**) take the **genitive**."
},
